          "title": "You'll want to know: గొడవపడు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గొడవపడు — goḍavapaḍu — \"to have a row; to quarrel\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చిన్న విషయానికి అన్నదమ్ములు గొడవపడ్డారు. cinna viṣayāniki annadammulu goḍavapaḍḍāru. The brothers had a row over a small thing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): గొడవపడ్డాను, goḍavapaḍḍānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "-తో గొడవపడు (goḍavapaḍu), to quarrel with."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "గొడవపడు (goḍavapaḍu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2048 lists Telugu goḍava, \"bother, worry, fuss\", with Kannada goḍave; the native verb paḍu, \"to feel, to suffer\" (DEDR 3853) makes the verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
