          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తగాదా — tagādā — \"a dispute; a row\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పొలం గురించి రెండు కుటుంబాల మధ్య తగాదా వచ్చింది. polaṁ guriñci reṇḍu kuṭumbāla madhya tagādā vaccindi. A dispute arose between two families over a field."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often about land or money."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తగాదా (tagādā) is usually traced to Arabic taqāḍā, \"a demand, a claim\", which came through Hindustani."
            }
          ]
        },
